    [Cherry-pick][releases/v0.30.0][BugFix] Fix SFA KV cache grouping and Prolog V3 indexer compatibility with pipeline parallelism (from #18167) (#18198)
    
    Cherry-pick of PR #18167 onto `releases/v0.30.0`.
    
    Original PR: #18167
    Original author: @YangShuai52
    
    ---
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    Tightens AscendMLAAttentionSpec.merge() validation to reject indexer
    specs during uniformity checks. The upstream caller can then select the
    appropriate cache grouping instead of raising AttributeError:
    'AscendSFAIndexerCacheSpec' object has no attribute
    'cache_sparse_sfa_c8'.
    Falls back to native preprocessing when the indexer query projection is
    unquantized. This prevents PROLOG_V3 from passing a quantized query to
    an indexer without weight_scale, including layers whose skip_topk state
    can change at runtime.
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
    Co-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>

